  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A narrow band of twisted weir-crawler gut, dyed in three fixed colours and worn high on the limb by everyone born within the same nine years. The colours give the grade and nothing else: there is no mark of rank, of household or of person, and two bands from the same grade are indistinguishable by design. Bands are made once, at the grade&#39;s forming, and are not replaced, so an old band is worn to a thread and is worn anyway. This one came from a grade whose span had ended and was handed over with the remark that it was now nothing.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
